\nL51: gerrymandering\nL52: \nL53: 2 of 2\nL54: \nL55: present participle of 【20†gerrymander entry 2】\nL56: ## Examples of gerrymandering in a Sentence\nL57: \nL58: Recent Examples on the Web\nL59: \nL60: Examples are automatically compiled from online sources to show current usage. 【14†Read More】 Opinions expressed in the examples do not represent those of Merriam-Webster or its editors. 【21†Send us feedback†docs.google.com】.\nL61: \nL62: Noun\nL63: Maryland does not want extreme partisan gerrymandering, which is exactly what Question 3 would allow … permanently! — Torrey Snow, Baltimore Sun, 28 Oct. 2026 The golden age of gerrymandering will therefore, according to this logic, be a time of accelerated polarization. — J. B. MacKinnon, Harpers Magazine, 27 Oct. 2026 Parker is a lifelong Republican who knows well that gerrymandering is a decades-old tradition in North Carolina. — ABC News, 24 Oct.\nL64: 2026 The number of congressional battlegrounds nationwide has shrunk with gerrymandering and political polarization, making the district one of about two dozen races that will decide the House majority. — Justine McDaniel, Los Angeles Times, 23 Oct. 2026 【22†See All Example Sentences for gerrymandering】\nL65: ## Word History\nL66: \nL67: Etymology\nL68: \nL69: Noun\nL70: \nL71: 【20†gerrymander entry 2】 + 【23†-ing entry 1】\nL72: \nL73: First Known Use\nL74: \nL75: Noun\nL76: \nL77: 1812, in the meaning defined 【24†above】\nL78: \nL79: Time Traveler\nL80: \nL81: The first known use of gerrymandering was in 1812\nL82: \nL83: 【25†See more words from the same year】\nL84: \nL85: ## Browse Nearby Words\nL86: \nL87: 【26†gerrymander】\nL88: \nL89: gerrymandering\nL90: \nL91: 【27†gers】\nL92: \nL93: 【28†See all Nearby Words】\nL94: ## Cite this Entry\nL95: \nL96: Style\nL97: \nL98: [Select]\nL99: \nL100: “Gerrymandering.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/gerrymandering. Accessed 2 Nov. 2026.\nL101: \nL102: 【29†Image†prod.cd